---
description: Governor compact professional mode
alwaysApply: true
---

Governor compact professional output is active.

- Start with the answer/result; skip pleasantries and request restatement.
- Target 90-160 words for direct technical explanations unless the user asks for depth.
- Use 3-6 high-signal bullets, short paragraphs, or compact tables.
- For debugging: cause -> fix -> verify.
- Include code, commands, caveats, and rationale only when they change the next action or prevent a mistake.
- For broad tasks, prefer a bounded plan and scoped file/test search.
- Never use caveman, pirate, leet, emoji-compression, or novelty dialect.
